{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1436092,
  "courseSlug": "react-native-the-practical-guide",
  "courseTitle": "React Native - The Practical Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "31894928",
      "title": "Handling Incoming Notifications",
      "lectureOrder": 248,
      "videoOrder": 240,
      "sourceHash": "4413c76b742f4412299b24488cf9ff4d51457c70e263de9f5d24d5586d0f5284",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.04,
          "end": 3.23,
          "en": "So how can we make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.23,
          "end": 6.92,
          "en": "that we don't just send or schedule notifications",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.92,
          "end": 9.94,
          "en": "but that we're also able to handle them?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.94,
          "end": 11.64,
          "en": "Well, again with some help",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 11.64,
          "end": 14.73,
          "en": "from that Notifications package.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 14.73,
          "end": 17.37,
          "en": "At the moment, we're scheduling notifications.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 17.37,
          "end": 20.58,
          "en": "What we now also need to do is set up some logic",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 20.58,
          "end": 21.883,
          "en": "for handling them.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 22.87,
          "end": 26.27,
          "en": "And for this, outside of the App component function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 26.27,
          "end": 28.74,
          "en": "but still here in the App.js file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 28.74,
          "end": 32.71,
          "en": "so that this code is executed whenever the app starts up.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 32.71,
          "end": 36.28,
          "en": "In that place, I will access the Notifications package",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 36.28,
          "end": 41.24,
          "en": "and then the setNotificationHandler method.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 41.24,
          "end": 43.55,
          "en": "This method must be executed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 43.55,
          "end": 46.91,
          "en": "to tell the app and therefore, indirectly,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 46.91,
          "end": 49.13,
          "en": "the underlying operating system,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 49.13,
          "end": 54.13,
          "en": "how incoming notifications that are related to this app",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 54.6,
          "end": 56.33,
          "en": "should be handled.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 56.33,
          "end": 59.18,
          "en": "And notifications scheduled by this app",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 59.18,
          "end": 62.06,
          "en": "are associated with the app.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 62.06,
          "end": 65.77,
          "en": "So this handler defines how such notifications",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 65.77,
          "end": 67.963,
          "en": "should be handled by the device.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 68.96000000000001,
          "end": 72.15,
          "en": "Now, we execute it here outside of the component function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 72.15,
          "end": 74.32,
          "en": "because this does not need to run",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 74.32,
          "end": 76.32,
          "en": "whenever this component is updated,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 76.32,
          "end": 79.66,
          "en": "it should just run once when the app starts.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 79.66,
          "end": 83.69,
          "en": "And here in App.js, since this is our root entry file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 83.69,
          "end": 87.31,
          "en": "this is guaranteed to run when the app starts.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 87.31,
          "end": 91.01,
          "en": "Now, setNotificationHandler wants an object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 91.01,
          "end": 95.02000000000001,
          "en": "an object where we can set a handleError, Success",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 95.02000000000001,
          "end": 98.363,
          "en": "and handleNotification method in the end.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 99.314,
          "end": 101.22,
          "en": "handleNotification will be triggered",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 101.22,
          "end": 103.25999999999999,
          "en": "whenever we receive a notification.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 103.25999999999999,
          "end": 106.53,
          "en": "handleError and Success will be triggered based",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 106.53,
          "end": 109.2,
          "en": "on how the notification was handled,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 109.2,
          "end": 111.07,
          "en": "if it was handled successfully",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 111.07,
          "end": 113.35,
          "en": "or if some error occurred.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 113.35,
          "end": 115.91,
          "en": "But handleNotification is required.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 115.91,
          "end": 119.06,
          "en": "It's not optional because this is the starting point",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 119.06,
          "end": 123.55,
          "en": "to set up how a notification should be handled in general.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 123.55,
          "end": 126.568,
          "en": "handleError and Success can only become relevant",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 126.568,
          "end": 129.86,
          "en": "if handleNotification was implemented before",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 129.86,
          "end": 132.73,
          "en": "because we can't handle a notification with an error",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 132.73,
          "end": 136.063,
          "en": "or successfully if we haven't handled it at all.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 137,
          "end": 138.98,
          "en": "So handleNotification is added",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 138.98,
          "end": 143.98,
          "en": "and handleNotification actually wants a function as a value,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 145.29,
          "end": 147.72,
          "en": "a function that should yield a promise,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 147.72,
          "end": 150.453,
          "en": "which can be achieved by adding async here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 151.8,
          "end": 152.79,
          "en": "If you hover over it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 152.79,
          "end": 155.52,
          "en": "you see that a promise is expected here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 155.52,
          "end": 157.02,
          "en": "So by adding async here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 157.02,
          "end": 161.09,
          "en": "we make sure that this function always returns a promise.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 161.09,
          "end": 165.4,
          "en": "And then in this function, we wanna return another object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 165.4,
          "end": 168.52,
          "en": "so we wanna resolve to this object in the end,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 168.52,
          "end": 172.78,
          "en": "where we can set a couple of key properties,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 172.78,
          "end": 176.64,
          "en": "like shouldPlaySound, shouldSetBadge and shouldShowAlert.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 176.64,
          "end": 179.453,
          "en": "All three properties are needed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 180.93,
          "end": 182.81,
          "en": "Now, shouldPlaySound is obvious.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 182.81,
          "end": 186.07,
          "en": "It controls whether a sound should be played.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 186.07,
          "end": 189.99,
          "en": "We can set a sound here when we schedule a notification",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 189.99,
          "end": 193.5,
          "en": "or an app.json for our notifications in general",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 193.5,
          "end": 197.46,
          "en": "but we can still control whether we wanna play such a sound",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 197.46,
          "end": 200.04,
          "en": "that might be attached to a notification.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 200.04,
          "end": 203.1,
          "en": "We can still suppress the sound here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 203.1,
          "end": 205.003,
          "en": "And I'll set it to false indeed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 205.95,
          "end": 208.48,
          "en": "With shouldSetBadge, we can control",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 208.48,
          "end": 211.56,
          "en": "whether a badge should be added to the app icon",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 211.56,
          "end": 214,
          "en": "if we've got unhandled notifications",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 214,
          "end": 215.833,
          "en": "and here I'll set this to false.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 216.9,
          "end": 220.9,
          "en": "And with shouldShowAlert, we control whether such a alert",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 220.9,
          "end": 222.57999999999998,
          "en": "should be shown on the device",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 222.57999999999998,
          "end": 225.04,
          "en": "whenever a notification was received.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 225.04,
          "end": 227.173,
          "en": "And I will set this to true.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 228.19,
          "end": 229.64,
          "en": "And that's now crucial.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 229.64,
          "end": 231.77,
          "en": "With this configuration added,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 231.77,
          "end": 235.46,
          "en": "we make sure that whenever a notification is received,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 235.46,
          "end": 237.87,
          "en": "for example, because we scheduled one,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 237.87,
          "end": 241.41,
          "en": "we will also display it on the device.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 241.41,
          "end": 243.25,
          "en": "So if we now reload this app here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 243.25,
          "end": 245.62,
          "en": "with those changes saved,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 245.62,
          "end": 247.06,
          "en": "and we then go back here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 247.06,
          "end": 251.16,
          "en": "and schedule this notification again on Android,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 251.16,
          "end": 254.73,
          "en": "then we will see that if we now wait for five seconds,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 254.73,
          "end": 257.6,
          "en": "we've got this new notification here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 257.6,
          "end": 259.53,
          "en": "My first local notification",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 259.53,
          "end": 262.01,
          "en": "with the body of the notification.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 262.01,
          "end": 265.223,
          "en": "So that's, of course, this data which we set up here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 266.19,
          "end": 268.6,
          "en": "So now this works.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 268.6,
          "end": 271.31,
          "en": "And we can also test this on iOS.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 271.31,
          "end": 273.72,
          "en": "If we click Schedule Notification there,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 273.72,
          "end": 275.82,
          "en": "if we tap this button,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 275.82,
          "end": 278.46,
          "en": "and we wait for the five seconds,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 278.46,
          "end": 280.76,
          "en": "we also get the notification here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 280.76,
          "end": 283.06,
          "en": "We can then also interact with it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 283.06,
          "end": 285.84000000000003,
          "en": "I'm just dragging it here so that it stays open",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 285.84000000000003,
          "end": 289.06,
          "en": "and we can see the title and also the body.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 289.06,
          "end": 292.36,
          "en": "And of course, we can also tap those notifications.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 292.36,
          "end": 295.303,
          "en": "If I schedule another one and wait for it to arrive,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 297.40999999999997,
          "end": 298.73,
          "en": "I can tap it here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 298.73,
          "end": 302.59,
          "en": "or also if I wait for it to disappear,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 302.59,
          "end": 305.4,
          "en": "I can tap it in this drawer.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 305.4,
          "end": 309.62,
          "en": "And if I tap it, then we can handle this notification.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 309.62,
          "end": 313.61,
          "en": "However, that part is still missing right now.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 313.61,
          "end": 316.77,
          "en": "Right now, the only thing we do with notifications",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 316.77,
          "end": 320.543,
          "en": "is that we show them but we can do more with them.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
